events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/zip","state":"uploaded","size":13746870,"digest":"sha256:7beaeb4743cf255809a8e574a2724c685b566545e04eabea284fe38a56c15b02","download_count":2333,"created_at":"2026-09-03T15:43:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T15:43:19Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/cli/cli/releases/download/v2.100.0/gh_2.100.0_windows_arm64.zip"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/tarball/v2.100.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/zipball/v2.100.0","body":"## Experimental: Route GitHub API traffic through a custom host\r\n\r\nOrganizations can now route a GitHub host's API traffic through a gateway using the new per-host `api_host` configuration:\r\n\r\n```shell\r\n# Route API traffic for github.com through a gateway\r\ngh config set api_host gh-gateway.example.com --host github.com\r\n\r\n# Read the configured API host\r\ngh config get api_host --host github.com\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe original host remains in use for authentication, Git remotes, and browser URLs.\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> `api_host` is experimental and is not a security boundary. Requests may still reach the original host.\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n\r\n### ✨ Features\r\n\r\n* Honor per-host `api_host` routing across GitHub API requests by @williammartin in [#14104](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14104)\r\n* Expose `api_host` through `gh config get` and `gh config set` by @williammartin in [#14332](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14332)\r\n* Add `webhook` as an official extension by @williammartin in [#14326](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14326)\r\n* Print full command help after command misuse when `gh` is invoked by a coding agent by @niik in [#14198](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14198)\r\n\r\n### 🐛 Fixes\r\n\r\n* fix(api): disable telemetry for unauthenticated GHES requests using absolute hostnames by @williammartin in [#14337](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14337)\r\n\r\n### 📚 Docs & Chores\r\n\r\n* Fix discussion acceptance test flags by @williammartin in [#14321](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14321)\r\n* Clarify supported GHES versions by @williammartin in [#14324](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14324)\r\n* Improve automated issue triage analysis by @sergiou87 in [#14318](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14318)\r\n* Record attachment counts in telemetry by @BagToad in [#14327](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14327)\r\n\r\n### :dependabot: Dependencies\r\n\r\n* chore(deps): bump `golang.org/x/crypto` from 0.55.0 to 0.56.0 by @babakks in [#14331](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14331)\r\n* chore(deps): bump Go toolchain from 1.26.7 to 1.26.8 by @babakks in [#14330](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14330)\r\n* chore(deps): bump `github.com/cli/go-gh/v2` from 2.15.0 to 2.16.0 by @williammartin in [#14338](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14338)\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/cli/cli/compare/v2.99.0...v2.100.0","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/releases/382143096/reactions","total_count":17,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":8,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":5,"eyes":0},"mentions_count":5}